<title>JAPAN: Japan says govt debt hit 334 trln yen at end-June.</title>
<headline>Japan says govt debt hit 334 trln yen at end-June.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Japanese government's outstanding debt, including that in the form of government bonds, totalled 334.1 trillion yen at the end of June, the Ministry of Finance (MOF) said in a statement on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Of the total, the outstanding amount of ordinary government bonds totalled 229.8 trillion yen at the end of June, it said.</p>
<p>A ministry official told reporters the ministry had decided to unveil the amount of outstanding national debt on a quarterly basis from now on.</p>
</text>
